        {
          "id": "87f0fe3a-b25e-4c60-9ab1-b5c726e4a3d9",
          "name": "Fit a Model",
          "request": {
            "name": "Fit a Model",
            "description": {
              "content": "**Deprecated:** Prefer the TabPFN client (`tabpfn-client`) or `POST /tabpfn/fit` after preparing uploads. This multipart `/v1/fit` surface is legacy. See the [TabPFN-3 changelog](/changelog/tabpfn-3).\n\nUploads and fits a TabPFN model on your training data. The API automatically handles preprocessing and stores a reference to your trained context (not the model weights). You can use either a single dataset file (with the target column included) or separate feature and label files.",
